# Viture Glasses — Gen1 HID protocol (Pro)

Applies when touching the Viture adapter: USB device detection, IMU pose
stream, control commands (recenter, brightness, display mode).

**Docs (if stuck):** https://github.com/bfvogel/viture-webxr-extension/blob/main/VITURE_PROTOCOL.md (Gen1 HID protocol write-up, works through Pro) ·
https://github.com/wheaney/XRLinuxDriver (protocol constants, display modes) ·
https://github.com/Droid-Deck/DroidDeck/pull/1115 (SDK-free 3DoF virtual screen on Android — prior art) ·
https://github.com/elasticjava/viture-v2/blob/master/PROTOCOL.md (Gen2; reference only — Pro is Gen1) ·
https://www.viture.com/developer/glasses-sdk/glasses (official SDK — proprietary, do NOT vendor)

## Device facts

- Composite USB device on the same USB-C link as DP video.
  VID **0x35CA**, Viture Pro PID **0x101D**. Several HID interfaces — dedupe,
  IMU and MCU control are separate interfaces.
- Owned Pro verified 2026-11-14 on SM-S948B. EDID name `VITURE`, PNP `CVT`,
  product id 12594, week 32 / 2023. Panel 1920×1080 @ 60 (active) / 90 / 120,
  dpi placeholder 25.4, HDR max 500 nits. USB strings: manufacturer
  `VITURE Pro`, product `N6P XR Glasses`, serial `208539935432`, config
  `Custom HID App`. Interfaces: 0 and 1 HID 64-byte interrupt in+out,
  2 CDC ACM, 3 CDC data bulk 64-byte. Dextop uid held `UsbManager` permission.
- Viture Pro: 1080p/eye, 2D modes 1920×1080 @ 60/90/120 (host-dependent),
  SBS 3840×1080 (we never drive SBS — 2D only). FOV ≈ 46° diagonal
  (~40°H × 23°V conservative), ~42 ppd.
- **No usable built-in 3DoF on Pro** — stabilization is always host-side.
- Android: video needs no permission; IMU/HID needs `UsbManager` runtime
  permission (user dialog or `device_filter.xml` vendor-id 13770). The XR
  permission broadcast action is `moe.n4tsu.dextop.xr.USB_PERMISSION` — do not
  reuse the Linux USB permission action. A dismissed dialog stays denied until
  an explicit UI re-request; do not ask again from a poll loop.

## Protocol notes (Gen1, measured on this Pro)

- Enable the glasses acked, 2026-11-14: 64-byte buffer, header `FF FE`,
  length field `0x0D` (`0x0C + payload`, little-endian), command `0x15` at
  offset 14, payload `01` at offset 18. No message counter. No `0x03` end
  marker. CRC-16/XMODEM (poly `0x1021`, init 0) stored little-endian at
  offset 2, over `lengthField + 2` bytes from offset 4. Opens
  `FF FE 27 25 0D 00 … 15 00 00 00 01`. The 20-byte CCITT packet was not
  required.
- IMU reports are `FF FC` on interface 0 interrupt IN. Three big-endian
  float32 degrees at offsets 18, 22, 26. This Pro's CRC locked to that same
  XMODEM little-endian check on the first report. Still probe CCITT-FALSE
  (init `0xFFFF`, stored big-endian) and lock whichever matches. Do not drop
  reports before the lock.
- MCU ack is `FF FD` on interface 1 interrupt IN. This Pro acked `0x15`
  immediately (`FF FD … 15 00`).
- Axis map in use: yaw = −degrees at 18, pitch = degrees at 26, roll =
  −degrees at 22, then radians. Resting sample before the origin subtract:
  yaw ~0.04 rad, pitch ~0.04 rad, roll ~2.90 rad. A head turn has not
  confirmed the signs.
- Claim interfaces 0 (IMU) and 1 (MCU) only, with `claimInterface(iface, true)`.
  Write commands on interface 1 OUT. Read both interrupt IN endpoints. Do
  not claim CDC interfaces 2 and 3.
- Recenter is the host origin reset. Do not send `0x30`. That id is the
  later SDK native-picture recenter, not the Gen1 IMU zero. Do not send
  display-mode or brightness commands.
- Measured pose rate: **62.8 Hz** over 5 seconds on SM-S948B. The community
  120–500 Hz range did not match this unit. Fusion must tolerate ~60 Hz
  and gaps.
- EDID changes on mode switches (HPD low/high) — some phones keep stale DP
  state → black screen or 640×480. Treat mode switches as disconnect/reconnect.

## Invariants

- Never vendor the official `libglasses.so` / SDK zip — proprietary, GPL-incompatible.
- Never toggle 2D/SBS or refresh from Dextop (decision: 2D only).
- Pose on this Pro is ~63 Hz, not the community 120–500 Hz range. Fusion
  must tolerate that rate and gaps.

## Symptom / cause / fix skeleton

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `0xFFFC` reports stop after a minute | IMU enable not retried after the interface re-opens | Re-send `0x15` on USB re-attach. Do not poll. |
| Enable write returns 64 and no IMU bytes arrive | Interrupt IN was read with bulkTransfer | Read interrupt IN with UsbRequest. On timeout, wait again on the same request. Do not clear or requeue it. |
| Reader dies at ~1s, or the next queue throws "currently queued" | `requestWait(timeout)` throws TimeoutException and leaves the request queued | Catch the timeout. Leave the request queued. |
| Next plug cannot claim the HID interfaces | Device closed while a request was still waiting | Cancel the request, join the reader, then send IMU-off and release interfaces 0 and 1. |
| CRC rejected | Wrong init or endian | This Pro matched XMODEM stored little-endian. Probe CCITT-FALSE big-endian and lock the first match. |
| Picture jumps when recenter is pressed | MCU `0x30` sent (SDK picture recenter) | Host origin reset only. Do not write `0x30`. |
| Black screen after refresh-rate change | Stale DP state across HPD/EDID change | Treat as reconnect; re-attach mirror on DisplayListener event |

